entage":0.658,"playId":"4018729651368","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6551,"playId":"4018729651398","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6424,"playId":"4018729651420","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6156,"playId":"4018729651443","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5592,"playId":"4018729651473","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5593,"playId":"4018729651484","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5435,"playId":"4018729651495","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5532,"playId":"4018729651529","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5219,"playId":"4018729651551","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5328,"playId":"4018729651576","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.5778,"playId":"4018729651598","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4873,"playId":"4018729651618","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4808,"playId":"4018729651654","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4892,"playId":"4018729651676","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4373,"playId":"4018729651698","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4333,"playId":"4018729651738","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4604,"playId":"4018729651775","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4643,"playId":"4018729651800","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.4647,"playId":"4018729651811","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"5534","guid":"022624d9-2dbd-3844-adab-9236c4319f9b","fullName":"Tottenham Hotspur Stadium","address":{"city":"London","country":"England"},"grass":true,"images":[]},"attendance":60907,"officials":[{"fullName":"Greg Bradley","displayName":"Greg Bradley","position":{"name":"Line Judge","displayName":"Line Judge","id":"113"},"order":1},{"fullName":"Paul King","displayName":"Paul King","position":{"name":"Umpire","displayName":"Umpire","id":"116"},"order":2},{"fullName":"Dale Shaw","displayName":"Dale Shaw","position":{"name":"Side Judge","displayName":"Side Judge","id":"115"},"order":3},{"fullName":"Alan Eck","displayName":"Alan Eck","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"114"},"order":4},{"fullName":"David Oliver","displayName":"David Oliver","position":{"name":"Down Judge","displayName":"Down Judge","id":"112"},"order":5},{"fullName":"Grantis Bell","displayName":"Grantis Bell","position":{"name":"Back Judge","displayName":"Back Judge","id":"110"},"order":6},{"fullName":"Anthony Flemming","displayName":"Anthony Flemming","position":{"name":"Field Judge","displayName":"Field Judge","id":"111"},"order":7}]},"article":{"headline":"Tea time as Jonathan Taylor runs for 2 TDs and Colts beat Commanders 30-13 in London","description":"— Sip some tea, score some touchdowns.","story":"LONDON -- — Sip some tea, score some touchdowns. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4242335/jonathan-taylor\">Jonathan Taylor</a>'s secret is out.\n\n\r\n              The Colts running back rushed for two touchdowns, quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3917792/daniel-jones\">Daniel Jones</a> also ran one in and Indianapolis beat Washington 30-13 after the Commanders lost yet another quarterback to injury on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Taylor said he enjoyed some tea at dinner on the eve of the game at Tottenham Hotspur Stadium. \n\n\r\n              And then <a href=\"https://x.com/Colts/status/2106758622516781152\">he mimicked the same</a> after one of his 5-yard touchdown runs to help the Colts (2-2) win their second straight game.\n\n\r\n              “I had to show the world, hey, I had a really good tea,” Taylor said.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota\">Marcus Mariota</a>, who was starting in place of the <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/jayden-daniels-mariota-starter-commanders-elbow-eb76e989cdf3bbc5a1e0b320e3fd74f4\">injured <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426348/jayden-daniels\">Jayden Daniels</a></a>, left the game after Washington’s second drive because of a knee injury. The veteran quarterback was sacked and didn’t return for the Commanders (1-3). \n\n\r\n              Coach Dan Quinn said it looks like an MCL injury and it's unknown how long he'll be out.\n\n\r\n              Third-string rookie quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432722/athan-kaliakmanis\">Athan Kaliakmanis</a> threw his first NFL touchdown pass to cut Indy's lead to 17-13 in the third quarter, but the Colts answered with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4571557/spencer-shrader\">Spencer Shrader</a>'s 52-yard field goal and Jones' 4-yard run early in the fourth quarter.\n\n\r\n              Taylor rushed for 95 yards on 20 carries as the Colts overcame two turnovers from Jones, who completed 19 of 34 passes for 143 yards with an interception and a fumble.\n\n\r\n              “Can’t afford to turn the ball over like that,” Jones said. “Got to understand when to take a chance, when not to, when to protect the ball, when you have a chance to make a play.”\n\n\r\n              Kaliakmanis threw a <a href=\"https://x.com/Colts/status/2106765905367605336\">costly interception</a> early in the third quarter and the Colts quickly capitalized. Linebacker <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4601021/jaylon-carlies\">Jaylon Carlies</a> picked off Kaliakmanis' pass at the Washington 27 and returned it to the 20. Taylor’s second 5-yard run of the game made it 17-6.\n\n\r\n              Kaliakmanis bounced back on the next drive, though, hitting <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4567156/treylon-burks\">Treylon Burks</a> on a 47-yard touchdown pass that closed the gap to 17-13. Burks got past cornerback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4427250/sauce-gardner\">Sauce Gardner</a> and found space before <a href=\"https://x.com/Commanders/status/2106769486535692303\">hauling in the deep ball</a>.\n\n\r\n              “It was surreal, man, it was absolutely surreal,” Kaliakmanis said, “but I've got to be honest, right now I'm just thinking about the loss. It's not about me. It's about this team.”\n\n\r\n              Shrader later added a 44-yard field goal — his third of the game — to extend Indy's lead to 30-13.\n\n\r\n              Kaliakmanis completed 15 of 33 passes for 186 yards with one touchdown and the interception.\n\n\r\n              The Colts led 10-6 at halftime after Taylor's first 5-yard touchdown run and then Shrader’s 48-yard field goal.\n\n\r\n              The Commanders failed to capitalize on two red zone opportunities in the first quarter, settling for field goals.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361422/odafe-oweh\">Odafe Oweh</a> drove Colts left tackle <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/colts-london-raimann-bynum-jonathan-taylor-e56607049581b214562bbbba42083c67\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4362580/bernhard-raimann\">Bernhard Raimann</a></a> backward into Jones causing the quarterback to fumble on Indy's first drive. Oweh then recovered it at the 21. The Commanders had fourth-and-2 from the 13 but opted for <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5081335/drew-stevens\">Drew Stevens</a>' 31-yarder.\n\n\r\n              Washington then stalled at the Colts 5 on their next drive. On third down, Mariota was sacked at the 11 by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4427635/adetomiwa-adebawore\">Adetomiwa Adebawore</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426473/laiatu-latu\">Laiatu Latu</a>. Mariota walked off gingerly to the sideline, and another Stevens field goal made it 6-0, but the quarterback didn't return.\n\n\r\n              Attendance was 60,907 for the 13th NFL game played at Tottenham. The league had recently <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/nfl-london-colts-commanders-ticket-price-reduced-b4fdf19231401e762bc99670f03d69e2\">reduced remaining ticket prices</a> to 79 pounds ($105) including for some high-end seats. Attendance has never been below 60,000 in previous games. The venue opened in 2019 and features an NFL field below the Premier League team’s <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o9kDe1eOn64\">moveable soccer pitch</a>. It was 70 degrees Fahrenheit at kickoff.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Global success</hl2>\r\n              Taylor's big day made him the <a href=\"https://x.com/Colts/status/2106798580870926466\">all-time leading rusher in NFL international games</a>, the Colts said. Taylor had rushed for 244 yards and three touchdowns last season in Indy's 31-25 overtime victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons\">Atlanta Falcons</a> in Berlin.\n\n\r\n              “I hope that I can continue to stack that, now that I’m apparently the leader,” Taylor said.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Injuries</hl2>\r\n              Colts: LT Bernhard Raimann was hurt early in the third quarter but returned.... WR <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4061956/ashton-dulin\">Ashton Dulin</a> and DE <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3843843/arden-key\">Arden Key</a> both sustained hamstring injuries.\n\n\r\n              Commanders: In addition to Mariota, WR <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4602667/jaylin-lane\">Jaylin Lane</a> had a “serious ankle injury,” Quinn said. DE <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3929865/charles-omenihu\">Charles Omenihu</a> had a groin problem... S <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4572460/tyler-owens\">Tyler Owens</a> left late with a hamstring injury.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Colts: at <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/pittsburgh-steelers\">Pittsburgh</a> next Sunday. \n\n\r\n              Commanders: host <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/new-york-giants\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/nyg/new-york-giants\">New York Giants</a></a> next Sunday. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nfl\">See AP’s full NFL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-04T17:08:27Z"}}